  "content": {
    "id": "p57-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find the coordinates of point $S$ where the tangent to the curve $y=x^2+4x-1$ is perpendicular to the line $4x+2y+7=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$S=\\left(-\\frac74,-\\frac{79}{16}\\right)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2y&=-4x-7\\\\y&=-2x-\\frac72\\end{align*}$$\nThe line has gradient $-2$, so the perpendicular tangent has gradient $-\\dfrac{1}{-2}=\\dfrac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=2x+4\\\\2x+4&=\\frac12\\\\2x&=-\\frac72\\\\x&=-\\frac74\\\\y&=\\left(-\\frac74\\right)^2+4\\left(-\\frac74\\right)-1\\\\&=\\frac{49}{16}-7-1\\\\&=-\\frac{79}{16}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $S=\\left(-\\dfrac74,-\\dfrac{79}{16}\\right)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
